"""E5 adapter for GLADMamba (ECML-PKDD 2025; github.com/Yali-Fu/GLADMamba @ 2b2462c, copied to ./src).

Same CLI and per-run JSON "part" schema as evalpaper/harness/run_eval.py, so the harness's
collect-style aggregation works on the parts (see ./collect.py).

One run = (GLADMamba, dataset, fold, hp) with hp in {ubgold, hpfree}:
  * ubgold : the authors' released per-dataset line (src/script/ad_<DS>.sh, parsed with the repo's own
             argparse parser, main.py:arg_parse); datasets without a released line (PROTEINS_full, MUTAG)
             use the modal released configuration (NOTES.md, "Hyperparameters").
  * hpfree : the repo's argparse defaults (main.py:18-47), except batch_size / batch_size_test which keep
             the per-dataset released value (A1 rule 2 analogue; NOTES.md).

The method's training and scoring code is used verbatim:
  * src/model.py is imported unchanged (GLADMamba, MambaBlock, RMSNorm, encoders, calc_loss_g/_n);
  * src/data_loader.py: get_ad_split_TU / get_ad_dataset_TU / init_structural_encoding /
    sparse_mx_to_torch_sparse_tensor are extracted with `ast` and executed unchanged;
  * src/main.py: arg_parse and setup_seed are extracted with `ast`; the per-trial training/evaluation loop
    (main.py:96-158) is copied line by line into fit() below.
Every deviation is marked "# CHANGE" and listed in NOTES.md.

At every evaluation point (epoch % eval_freq == 0, plus the final epoch) we record test AUROC/AUPRC/FPR95
(UB-GOLD's metric functions = sklearn, as GLADMamba's own skm.roc_auc_score), per-graph test scores in
canonical test order, and the per-graph anomaly scores of the 20% held-out normal training graphs
(RandomState(2026 + 1000*fold), identical to the harness); their mean is "holdout_score" (VAL-NORMAL, A3).

Usage:
  PYTHONDONTWRITEBYTECODE=1 python -B run_method.py --method GLADMamba --dataset BZR --fold 0 [--hp hpfree]
"""
